WEBVTT

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.580
Are those two going to be okay?

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.280
A switch created by nature,
a natural mechanism...

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.240
A mysterious tower created 
by Mother Nature...

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.500
That's impossible!

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.890
What is this place?

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:09.270
"Episode 10: Feelings Overlapping"

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.980
Who would make a place like this?

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.380
We're in the middle of the mountain, right?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:15.860
I know I said nobody's really taken
a look at Mt. Sankaku yet, but this is...

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.310
The underground base of
Gelgey the Fiend was just like this!

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.590
Gelgey...

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.120
Gelgey the Fiend is...

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.770
...the powerful ruler 
of an evil organization.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:37.130
He forces the innocent
to engage in harsh labor...

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:40.680
Should I punch you again to wake you up?

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.550
It was a joke.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.580
But well, you may not be that far off.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.980
Look.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.790
This place was probably
a combination of prison and mine.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:59.240
I've never seen a design like this.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.910
Well, it's probably really old...

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:06.850
No, it's probably not in
any history book, either.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.260
We can go through there, I think.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.160
A dead end?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.210
What's that?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.690
A crown... I think, anyway.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.960
But well... it goes in here, right?

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.540
What's that sound?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.650
Who knows?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.730
A hidden passage?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.510
What kind of high-tech maze is this place?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.700
I'll go on ahead.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.350
You follow behind me.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:15.010
Another body!

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:17.380
Calm down.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.750
S-Sorry...

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.060
Was he one of the workers here?

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:32.310
It looks like the letters on Futago Rock.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.520
Boss, look...

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.730
That's Mio's!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.810
Shimazu-<i>san</i>...

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.450
That notebook she always
kept with her isn't here.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.970
Was she here, looking at these letters?

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:59.550
That means she's lost down here somewhere,
with no water and no food, right?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.610
Yeah, this isn't good. We need to hurry.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.370
Shimazu-<i>san</i>! Shimazu-<i>san</i>!

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.280
Wait, Yuki!

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.540
--Shimazu-<i>san</i>!
--Wait, I said!

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:25.450
Yuki! Yuki!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.650
Shit!

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.230
Yuki!

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:36.710
Where are you?!

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.660
Answer me!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.030
Boss...

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.210
Yuki!

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:48.480
You're...

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.250
Hang in there!

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:53.990
I'll get you out of that...

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:59.000
Boss, worry about Shimazu-<i>san</i>, not me...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.380
You idiot!

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.340
What are you saying?

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.840
Please!

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.330
It's my fault...

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.320
It's my fault Shimazu-<i>san</i>...

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.720
Stop talking. Calm down!

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.360
I'll get Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.380
Please... Save Shimazu-<i>san</i>!

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.650
You're kidding me...

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.320
Wake the hell up, Yuki!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.740
Wake up! Wake up, Yuki!

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:34.610
Come on!

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.840
No... This can't be real...

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.490
Yuki! Wake up!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.030
Say something stupid!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:07:00.030
A world where Yuki dies... has to be a lie!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.160
Listen for a second.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:14.930
What's up?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.030
You need to stay here after all.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.080
Why, boss?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.080
You just said you'd go with me!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.400
I stopped to think about it,
and you're still not calmed down.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.430
You'll just get in the way.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.010
B-But it's my fault!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.430
So I need to save her myself!

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:37.770
You'll just get in the way!

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.340
I don't have time to look
after someone who can't help.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.460
Let's go, Mitsuki-<i>san</i>.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.600
Okay.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.370
That's just like you, Takuya.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.210
What's this about?

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.380
You were that harsh to
him deliberately, weren't you?

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.290
That's not it.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.540
He's clumsy, that's why he gets kill--

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.050
Nothing.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.550
Anyway, I think it's around here...

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:16.730
There we go.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.390
How did you know that was there?

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.850
Well, you see it all the time in video games.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.450
Let's keep going.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.400
Is this Shimazu-<i>san</i>'s bag?

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:41.790
I think so.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.830
What's that sound?

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:49.280
This isn't what happened
in the last parallel world.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:52.910
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.310
Oww...

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.850
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>, are you okay?

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.360
Yeah, I think so.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.440
But I lost my flashlight.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.940
Me too.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.730
Shit... where did it go?

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.110
Don't take off my skirt!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:21.460
Sorry.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.460
Sheesh...

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.040
It was too dark to see...

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.500
Now's not the time for this!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.290
I know that.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.360
Look, I think there's something here.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.050
Don't try and touch my breasts
when I can't see you!

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.860
It wasn't deliberately.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:41.390
Man, your body is as sensitive as ever, huh?

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.250
Here we go.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:46.950
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:52.690
I knew Mitsuki-<i>san</i> was getting old,
but I didn't think she'd turn into a mummy!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.110
Shut up.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:56.410
Sorry.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.950
Is that somebody who got lost down here?

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.080
I don't know...

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.360
It seems newer than the other bodies...

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.010
"Yurika Imagawa"

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.100
This belonged to Dr. Yurika Imagawa!

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:21.210
Dr. Imagawa? Didn't she work with my dad?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.270
Yeah.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.810
I heard she went missing...

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.030
I guess this is where she ended up.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.130
What's it say?

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:34.980
"The fear and anticipation 
threatens to crush me.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:40.580
Even as I write these words,
I'm shaking like a child.

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:48.290
It's possible that the key to history's greatest
mysteries lies here in Mt. Sankaku.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.500
These ruins have been here for millennia.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:56.100
I regret the fact that
I couldn't bring a whole team.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:02.150
These ruins are different from
those of any culture in history.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:06.750
Perhaps this must have been
caused by an event collision between

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:10.260
two dimensions that crossed the boundaries."

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.040
Event collision?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:19.660
"Dr. Arima's theory was that event
collisions occurred every 400 years.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:24.160
For example, Takanoamahara, which exists
on a different dimension than our own,

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.700
was involved in an event 
collision with Japan,

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.110
resulting in the importation 
of a new culture.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.630
I investigated the electromagnetic
and gravitational fields of Sakaimachi,

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:39.660
and concluded that indeed, an event
collision had taken place in the past.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.480
What causes an event collision?

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.870
I was so eager to solve the mystery,

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.630
that I foolishly let myself get to
the point where I can no longer go on.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.650
But my heart remains filled 
with pure curiosity.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.800
This feeling... yes, it reminds
me of that moment.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:08.630
When Dr. Arima gave it to me.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.980
I still can't forget it...

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:17.750
The moment I held that strange device
to which I would later give the name...

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:23.290
...'Reflector Device.'"

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:27.740
The light...

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.690
The Reflector Device...

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.060
You have it, don't you?

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.900
What are you talking about?

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:45.070
Let me see it.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.810
That's Ryuzoji's...

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.080
Give it here. Now.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.290
Takuya...

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.550
Be a good boy.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:56.480
I can't do that.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.480
My dad entrusted this to me.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:01.520
I see.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.630
You leave me no choice then.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:15.680
Next time I'll aim for your head.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:19.310
Hurry. Now give me the reflector device!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:23.510
Hurry...

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.530
Is it the Niarb?

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.620
I have to shoot you...

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.710
But I don't want to!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.870
But I have to!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.620
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.680
Ryuzoji is controlling you!

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.760
Get a hold of yourself!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:45.270
If he wants it, I'll get it for him...

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:49.050
That's my job!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.230
I won't let you get away!

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.960
Whew!

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:06.990
What's that?

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:08.560
A coffin?

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.120
Takuya!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.380
Where are you?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.090
Crap!

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.500
Hide-and-seek?

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.310
I'll find you very, very soon!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.110
What is this light?

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.330
Wake up!

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.360
Wake up!

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.550
Just five more minutes... please...

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:24.690
I said wake up!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.800
Arima-<i>kun</i>!

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.910
That hurt!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.740
Oww!

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:37.790
Hey!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.580
I'm glad you're safe.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.380
I knew a history nut like
you wouldn't die that easily.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.880
That's a very rude way to put it.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.280
Did you get hurt?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:53.650
No... My butt's a little cold, though.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:57.510
Okay, I'll rub it and warm it up for you.

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.020
No, thank you!

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.020
I thought I was a goner.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:08.190
But I had a feeling you'd come.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.010
It took me a while, though.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.780
Anyway, this is a strange place.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.110
A glowing underground lake...?

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:23.170
It looks like the rocks
under the lake are glowing.

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:24.670
Glowing rocks?

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.380
Psychite?

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.660
What's wrong?

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:32.990
Nothing.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.870
Let's find the exit.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.810
We should be able to, with two people.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.700
Where do I even begin?

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:45.830
Start by telling me your measurements.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:49.130
I always thought that 
the Takanoamahara people

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:52.250
were related to Mt. Sankaku somehow.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:57.240
But these ruins were much older than that...

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:01.250
Yes. So I want to do a real investigation,

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.830
and solve the mysteries
of the Japanese people...

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:07.580
No, all humanity.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:13.850
Actually, Dr. Imagawa's notes
said the same thing.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.890
You read them, right?

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.240
Yes. I found them in the cave.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:24.050
Her theory about event collisions
was especially shocking to me...

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.460
She said that one dimension
might collide with another.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:32.080
And you think it's real?

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:37.570
It's hard to believe, but if it's real,

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:42.120
it explains why there's a civilization here
that's not found in our history.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:47.040
That sound again...

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.470
Watch out!

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:55.660
Mio!

00:17:58.310 --> 00:17:59.150
Grab on.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.490
Boss... Shimazu-<i>san</i>...

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.800
You okay?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.650
Don't stare at me, dummy!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.340
I'll look for the exit.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.230
You get some rest.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.440
Wait!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.290
Don't leave me here.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:32.290
But...

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.660
You won't find the exit.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.320
I looked everywhere myself.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:41.450
Please...

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.280
Don't leave me alone.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.400
Those papers that went up...

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.860
...on the bulletin board this morning.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:58.880
You didn't do it, did you?

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:03.440
Sorry. I did it.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:05.760
What?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.900
I knew you'd say that.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.100
It was Yuki-<i>kun</i>, wasn't it?

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:15.050
No! Did he tell you he did?

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:20.360
No. I could tell when I talked to him.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.430
He's a terrible liar.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.940
I hit him before I came down here.

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.890
I won't say that's a
good reason to forgive him,

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.630
but... don't blame him too much.

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.130
I guess that's too much to ask for.

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:45.450
No. I was really hurt when I saw them,

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:47.660
but what those papers said was true.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:52.210
People would've found out what
my dad was doing eventually...

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:57.230
And I think he should be
punished for what he did, too...

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.860
Hey, are you okay?

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:06.400
Will we die down here, you think?

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.870
Of course not.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:11.860
Yuki's waiting outside.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.150
When we don't come back
he'll go to the police...

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.190
Arima-<i>kun</i>...

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:20.450
Kiss me.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:27.580
I want one last thing
to remember... before I die.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:29.730
Please!

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.750
This won't be the last thing you remember.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.280
We're leaving here alive.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.960
Alive. Got it?

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.880
Should I head back?

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.950
But I don't remember
the path I took to get here,

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:18.900
and I don't know that
I'll be able to see Mio again.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:23.470
I'll rest a bit and
then look for the exit again.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:36.820
Takuya...

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:40.730
Takuya...

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.330
Don't worry.

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:51.920
Takuya...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.660
I'm here with you.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.080
Mother?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:41.530
"Episode 11: That Kiss, Once More"

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:39.340
Episode 11: "That Kiss, Once More."
